cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or reference this specification, please cite it as below."
title: "Zero-trust AI operations: specification"
abstract: >-
  Zero-trust AI operations is zero trust applied to the AI that runs IT
  operations: the AI gets the reach, and never the trust. This open,
  vendor-neutral specification sets out five rules as testable requirements:
  act only as the person who asked, never give the AI a credential, give it no
  network of its own, let only a person approve a change exactly as it will
  run, and record every decision where the AI cannot change it. It includes a
  threat model, the residual risk a conforming system still carries, a
  conformance guide, a crosswalk to NIST SP 800-207, the OWASP Top 10 for LLM
  and for Agentic Applications 2026 and the Model Context Protocol, and a
  checklist for buyers. This version is a draft for public review.
